00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.240
have calculated in this. But you get a

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.800
return in the stock market of of 80K of

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.720
10% annualized on 5 years. There's

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.200
actually no interest rate you pay over

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.320
here because we're not taking out a

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.760
loan, we're just taking the straight

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:07.680
cash. So, that means over [music]

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.080
a 5-year period, we're going to have

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.920
about 128K. But, let's look at [music]

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.760
option number two. We have the same

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.760
amount of money to start, 100K in stock,

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.200
but instead of taking the money out

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.320
directly, we take 20K out in a loan.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.040
This is called a securities backed line

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.840
of credit or an SBLOC. [music]

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.480
The bank can actually give you this

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.480
$20,000.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.360
You still own the $100,000 portfolio,

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.360
