00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.400
almost anything. You can use it as a

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:45.360
down payment on a house, on a business,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.320
a tax bill. What's interesting here, you

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.680
still have an interest rate of 6%.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.120
You're going to have a return of 10%,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.840
but look at this. The 100K compounds to

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.760
161K

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.480
over this period. You will be subtract

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.320
the 6K in annual interest, and then

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.400
we're going to pretend like we didn't

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.000
make more money with the 20K, so we're

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.760
just going to pay back the loan. Even in

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:08.200
the case where the 20K does nothing for

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:10.640
us, we make 135K here instead of 128K

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:13.000
here. Now, over time, if this continues

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.280
to compound, it gets really sexy. So,

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.920
the difference between taking out a loan

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:21.280
and selling a piece of your asset comes

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.440
down to a pretty decent return here. And

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.320
that's the billionaire strategy of Elon

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.600
Musk and Larry Ellison. They're not

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.602
actually selling their golden goose

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.320
ever. They are borrowing against it.

00:03:29.602 --> 00:03:33.480
[music] And if the asset grows faster

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:36.519
than the cost of debt, aka the interest

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.400
rate here, then the math works. Okay, so

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:40.082
if you're clever, you're going to say,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.920
"How do you pay the interest payments?"

00:03:40.082 --> 00:03:43.760
[music] That's where you use your salary

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.440
or your business cash flow to cover the

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.840
interest, this [music] 6%, just like you

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.959
